  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 1230 PM CST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nThe long-term continues to be dry through mid-week next week, thanks \nto the high pressure system remaining anchored over the central \nCONUS, along with amplified upper-level ridging over the \nIntermountain West states. The main focus for this time frame will \nbe on temperatures as they look to become above average. By Monday, \nhigh temperatures are forecast to rise to the middle 60s, which \nwould be nearly 10 degrees above average for this time of the year. \nMild conditions will last through Wednesday before cooling down \nThursday as guidance is indicating a longwave trough to move through \nthe area. NBM isn't suggesting any precipitation at this time \n(although we can't rule it out entirely), but rather, a bit more \ncloud cover resulting from it.",
